The bug occurs because the original code checks both the presence of a token file location and whether security is enabled. When security is off, the condition fails, preventing the loading of necessary tokens, which breaks the functionality of the MapReduce framework. By removing the security check, the code allows for the correct operation of MR even when security is disabled.

